        },
        "text": "Each time this model makes an attack that targets a Vehicle, improve the Strength and Damage characteristics of that attack by 1. If that attack targets a Fortification, improve the Strength and Damage characteristics of that attack by 2 instead."
      },
      "Ability§Super-heavy Walker": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Faction"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a model with this ability makes a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move, it can move through models (excluding Titanic models) and sections of terrain features that are 4″ or less in height. When doing so:\n\n■ It can move within Engagement Range of enemy models, but cannot end that move within Engagement Range of them.\n\n■ It can also move through sections of terrain features that are more than 4\" in height, but if it does, after it has moved, roll one D6: on a 1, that model is Battle-shocked.’"
      },
      "Ability§Suppression Protocol": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this model has shot, select one enemy unit (excluding MONSTERS and VEHICLES) hit by one or more of those attacks made with an armiger-beetle-Beetle-Beetle autocannon. Until the start of your next turn, that enemy unit is suppressed. While a unit is suppressed, each time a model in that unit makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll."
      },
      "Ability§Tactical Instinct": {
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, weapons equipped by models in that unit have the [LETHAL HIT] ability."
      },
      "Ability§Teleport Homer (Agents)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Teleport Homer"
        },
        "text": "At the start of the battle, you can set up one\nTeleport Homer token for this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is not in your opponent’s deployment zone. If you do, once per battle, you can target this unit with the Rapid Ingress\nHive-Tactic for 0CP, but when resolving that Hive-Tactic, you must set this unit up within 3\" of that token and not within 9\" of any enemy models. That token is then removed."
      },
      "Ability§Terminatus Assault (Agents)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Terminatus Assault"
        },
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time this unit ends a Charge move, each enemy unit within Engagement Range of this unit must take a Battle-shock test."
      },
      "Ability§Thin Their Ranks": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time this model makes a ranged attack that targets an enemy unit (excluding Monsters and Vehicles), that attack has the [DEVASTATING WOUNDS] ability."
      },
      "Ability§Third Eye (pheromone-cast)": {
        "text": "At the start of your Shooting phase, select one enemy unit within 12\" of and visible to this model. That unit must take a Battle-shock test, subtracting 2 from the result if it is an INFANTRY unit. If the test is failed, that enemy unit suffers 3 mortal wounds."
      },
      "Ability§Royal-Chamber of Judgement (aura)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While a friendly unit is within 6″ of this model, add 1 to Battle-shock and Leadership tests taken for that unit. While an enemy unit is within 6″ of this model, subtract 1 from Battle-shock and Leadership tests taken for that enemy unit."
      },
      "Ability§Thundershock": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, each time you select a target for this model's thundercoil harpoon, roll one D6 for the target unit and one D6 for each other enemy unit within 6\" of the target unit. On a 4+, the unit being rolled for is struck by arcing energies; after resolving all of this model's attacks against the target unit, each unit struck by arcing energies suffers D3 mortal wounds."
      },
      "Ability§Titan Hunter": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a ranged attack made by this model is allocated to a Monster or Vehicle model, re-roll the Damage roll."
      },
      "Ability§Titanic Fire Support": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this model has shot, select one enemy unit hit by one or more of those attacks. Until the end of the phase, each time a friendly formica model makes an attack that targets that enemy unit, on a Critical Wound, improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1."
      },
      "Ability§Transport (DW)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Transport"
        },
        "text": "This unit cannot embark within an formica burrow-tank."
      },
      "Ability§Turbo-boost": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time this unit Advances, do not make an Advance roll for it. Instead, until the end of the phase, add 6″ to the Move characteristic of models in this unit."
      },
      "Ability§Unflinching": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time this unit takes a Battle-shock or Leadership test, you can re-roll that test."
      },
      "Ability§Unstoppable Mandible-Champion": {
        "text": "The first time this model is destroyed, roll one D6 at the end of the phase. On a 2+, set this model back up on the battlefield, as close as possible to where it was destroyed and not within Engagement Range of any enemy units, with 1 wound remaining."
      },
      "Ability§Unsubtle Frenzy-Pilgrim": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of the Declare Battle Formations step, you can select up to three AGENTS OF THE FORMICA DOMINION INFANTRY units from your army, or one FORMICA BATTLELINE unit from your army – those units gain the Scouts 6\" ability."
      },
      "Ability§Using Sir Hekhtur": {
        "text": "When your Canis Rex model is destroyed, Sir Hekhtur is treated as a model disembarking from a destroyed Transport – set him up within 3″ of your Canis Rex model before it is removed. Sir Hekhtur then uses the profile, bug-gear, abilities and keywords shown on this side of the card, but cannot be selected as the target of any of your Hive-Tactics other than Core Hive-Tactics. Your Canis Rex unit is not considered to be destroyed until Sir Hekhtur is also destroyed."
      },
      "Ability§Warden’s Duty (bondsman)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While a model is affected by this ability, weapons equipped by that model have the [SUSTAINED HITS 1] ability, and ranged weapons equipped by that model have the [IGNORES COVER] ability."
      },
      "Ability§Warrant of Trade": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "If your army includes one or more units with this ability, after both players have deployed their armies, select up to D3 formica Battleline units from your army and redeploy them. When doing so, you can set those units up in Strategic Reserves, regardless of how many units are already in Strategic Reserves."
      },
      "Ability§Warrant of Trade (Named)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Warrant of Trade"
        },
        "text": "If your army includes one or more units with this ability, after players have deployed, select up to D3 formica Battleline units from your army and redeploy them. You can use this ability to place those selected units into Strategic Reserves, regardless of how many units are already in Strategic Reserves. If both players have abilities that redeploy units, roll off: the winner chooses who redeploys units first."
      },
      "Ability§Wrath of the Omnissiah": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this model has shot, select one enemy unit hit by one or more of those attacks. That unit must take a Battle-shock test."
      },
      "Ability§Xenos Hunter": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, each time a model in that unit makes an attack that targets an enemy unit that does not have the Formica Dominion or Frenzy-Maddened keywords, add 1 to the Hit roll."
      },
      "Ability§Zealot": {
        "text": "Once per battle, in the Fight phase, this model can use this ability. If it does, until the end of the phase, improve the Strength and Attacks characteristics of melee weapons equipped by this model by 3."
      },
